[00:14.56]Old man wakes before the sun
[00:21.24]Salt and wrinkles,
[00:23.11]he's the only one
[00:28.12]Wooden boat with a broken sail
[00:34.51]He sets his course through the morning pale
[00:41.51]Eighty days with nothing on the line
[00:45.16]Every cast he throws against the tide
[00:48.49]Hands are shaking but he holds on tight
[00:52.07]Something big is swimming through the night
[00:56.79]Hold the line,
[00:59.60]don't let it go
[01:00.85]The sea is deep,
[01:01.67]the wind will blow
[01:10.45]One more pull before the dawn
[01:17.21]This old heart will carry on
[01:21.56]Stars are gone,
[01:22.10]the sky is grey
[01:23.18]Blisters burning but he will not stray
[01:34.91]Sharks are circling,
[01:35.55]taking what they can
[01:39.70]Still he sails back to the sand
[01:44.42]Hold the line,
[01:47.19]don't let it go
[01:50.90]The sea is deep,
[01:54.17]the wind will blow
[01:57.95]One more pull before the dawn
[02:04.69]This old heart will carry on
[02:38.80]Hold the line,
[02:41.45]don't let it go
[02:45.08]The sea is deep,
[02:48.31]the wind will blow
[02:52.10]One more pull before the dawn
[02:58.86]This old heart will carry on
[03:03.06]He comes home with only bones
[03:11.09]But his spirit stands alone
[03:14.52]Waves will whisper what he's done
[03:18.55]Underneath the setting sun